Z||000000||bcwawright||06-03-2001||12:34 PM||||Does Pontiac still sell interior trim pieces, door and window weatherstripping, inner and out dew strips, emergency brake lever assembly, etc.<BR>Thanks in advance<P>Bruce<BR>88GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||Bob Englert||06-03-2001||02:53 PM||||It is difficult to give you a direct answer, since the parts appear to be shrinking almost daily.  The best bet is to check with the local Pontiac dealer or do a part number search on gmpartsdirect.com.  Someone on the forum can probably look up a parts number in the 22P book.<P>Last time I checked dew strips are still available, but little or no interior trim is still available.  Some switches might be available.  I have found a lot of items that could be found 1 or 2 years ago are now out of stock.  <P>GM did recently restock the GT quarter windows.  Otherwise, most parts just seem to disappear.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||06-04-2001||09:30 AM||||When I went to a local Pontiac dealer to get a Input Shaft Bearing for my Getrag, they told me GM didn't stock Fiero parts anymore and he then handed me a Fiero Store catalog!  He said GM sold all their stock to them.  ||||reg||6
